// A dialect program that names the dialect (ui::WEB) and `stderr` itself,
// including nothing. Bound or parsed live, it emits the same C: its own
// `stderr` is the compiler's stream, `__madc_stdio_stream(2)` — never a
// restored `extern void *stderr;` frozen from a dialect TU's own stand-in
// (the stand-in is the compiler's declaration, not a record).
// Oracle: C11 7.21.1p3 — stderr is an expression of type FILE *; the C
// analogue (`#include <stdio.h>`, fputs to stderr, the printf line) behaves the same
// under gcc 13 and clang 18. The emitted C is the observable: the defect
// was bind-only (the packed binary), the run's output identical.
int main(void)
{
	long level = ui::WEB;
	fputs("user stderr line\n", stderr);
	printf("web above tui: %d\n", level > ui::TUI ? 1 : 0);
	return 0;
}
